==English==
{{was wotd|2017|August|28}}

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|fr|syndicat||[[office]] of a [[syndic]]; [[board]] of syndics; [[trade union]]}}, from {{m|fr|syndic||syndic; [[representative#Noun|representative]]; chief [[magistrate]] of [[Geneva]]}} + {{m|fr|-at||''suffix denoting an action or result of an action''}}, from {{der|en|ML.|*syndicatus}}, from {{m|la|syndicus||representative of a [[corporation]] or [[town]]; syndic}} (from {{der|en|grc|σύνδικος||[[advocate#Noun|advocate]] for a [[defendant]]}}, from {{m|grc|σύν||[[beside]]; [[with]]}} + {{m|grc|δίκη||[[judgment]]; [[justice]]}}) + {{m|la|-ātus||''suffix forming adjectives from nouns indicating the possession of a thing or a quality''}}.

Compare {{cog|it|sindacato||syndicate; trade union; [[audit#Noun|audit]], [[control#Noun|control]], [[supervision]]}}, {{cog|oc|sendegat}}, {{cog|pt|sindicato||trade union}}, {{cog|es|sindicado}}, {{m|es|sindicato||office of a syndic; syndicate; trade union}}.

===Pronunciation===
* Noun: {{a|RP|GA}} {{IPA|/ˈsɪndɪkət/|lang=en}}
* Verb: {{a|RP|GA}} {{IPA|/ˈsɪndɪkeɪt/|lang=en}}
* {{hyphenation|syn|dic|ate|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[group]] of [[individual#Noun|individuals]] or [[company|companies]] formed to [[transact]] some specific [[business]], or to [[promote]] a common [[interest#Noun|interest]]; a self-[[coordinate#Verb|coordinating]] group.
#: {{ux|en|a gambling '''syndicate'''}}
## {{lb|en|crime}} A group of [[gangster]]s engaged in [[organized crime]].
## {{lb|en|mass media}} A group of [[media]] companies, or an [[agency]], formed to [[acquire]] [[content#Noun|content]] such as [[article]]s, [[cartoon]]s, etc., and to [[publish]] it in [[multiple]] [[outlet]]s; a [[chain#Noun|chain]] of newspapers or other media outlets [[manage]]d by such an [[organization]].
# The [[office]] or [[jurisdiction]] of a [[syndic]]; a [[body]] or [[council]] of syndics.
#: {{rfquotek|Bishop Burnet}}

